E[18]['result']['proof']+=' The finite-height qualification is mathematical, not merely computational: an enclosure on a compact x-interval cannot exclude a new critical point or sign change beyond that interval. To pass to all heights, one needs uniform lower bounds or an independently controlled tail that dominates every remainder. Shrinking α also amplifies μ like1/α, so transporting the unrenormalized masses with a fixed absolute error budget is intrinsically ill-conditioned. The finite limit of αμ suggests the correct unknown to enclose, but does not itself prove positivity of the full renormalized kernel.'
E[7]['result']['proof']+=' For normalized coefficients the entropy formula is obtained by listing every squared singular value of a block as p_j s_{j,k}, withΣ_k s_{j,k}=1. Expanding−Σ_{j,k}p_js_{j,k}log(p_js_{j,k}) separates the sector entropy−Σp_jlogp_j from the average within-sector entropy. This calculation shows exactly why probabilities, rather than unnormalized block ranks, enter the entropy identity.'
more={
0:' The same projectors compute every polynomial observable: h(T)=Σh(λ)E_λ. For z outsideS they also give the exact resolvent(zI−T)^{-1}=ΣE_λ/(z−λ), verified by multiplication. Thus the certificate supplies inversion and spectral decomposition, not just an eigenvalue list. Its denominators are explicit rational differences between distinct roots.',
1:' The finite quotient has maximal ideal generated byu,v, with square spanned byv² and cube zero. Its socle containsu andv² and has dimension two. Consequently its symmetric Hilbert function does not make it a Gorenstein algebra: the multiplication pairing from degree one to the top degree is degenerate becauseu annihilates both generators.',
2:' The alternating graded resolution gives Hilbert numerator1−2t²−t³+t³+t⁴=1−2t²+t⁴. Dividing by(1−t)² yields1+2t+t². The cancellation of the two degree-three terms in this numerical series conceals their distinct homological origins, which is why the Hilbert series alone cannot decide whether the displayed resolution is a complete intersection.',
3:' Tensoring the socles also gives a direct type certificate: the only elements killed byx,y,z are scalar combinations ofxz andy²z. Their independence follows from the eight standard monomials. Hence the last free-module rank two matches a genuinely two-dimensional socle, and the symmetric Hilbert function cannot rescue a proposed Gorenstein interpretation.',
5:' Each independent binary commutation equation halves the number of solutions. If the support span has rankr, the kernel therefore contains exactly2^{2n−r} Pauli labels. This is a count of Pauli symmetries modulo scalar phase, not automatically the dimension of the full operator commutant ofH; degeneracies may create further linear combinations of operators commuting withH.',
6:' The character-shift map is linear overF₂, so all nonempty fibres have the same size2^{dim(G∩Q⊥)}. Its image acts freely by translations on the character labels, and the orbit size is exactly the image cardinality. This proves the sector-count statement through an explicit action, without conflating the stabilizer with an unrelated isotropic subgroup.',
8:' Square-freeness matters because the discriminant of an order equals the field discriminant times its index squared. Since23 has no square factor, the orderZ[t] cannot have index larger than one. This argument proves maximality of the order, but does not identify a fundamental unit: a visible unit might be a proper power of another unit.',
9:' The initialq factor proves vanishing at the cusp∞ because the remaining product has constant term one and converges forImτ>0. It does not by itself check every cusp ofΓ₀(23), nor the full character law. Those require the eta-quotient transformation theorem or separate cusp calculations, rather than an inference from the two displayed transformations alone.',
12:' Distributionally the sign follows by integration by parts on the two half-lines: the smooth terms cancel againstG itself and the boundary contribution is−[G′]₀φ(0)=φ(0) for a test functionφ. This explains why a derivative jump, not a pointwise second derivative atzero, carries the Dirac source in a Green kernel.',
13:' The weight count distinguishes a representation from a Lie-algebra construction. To recoverE₈ one must define anso₁₆-equivariant mapΛ²S⁺→so₁₆, choose its normalization and verify the Jacobi identity for triples of spinors. Dimension agreement and a plausible root count are strong consistency checks but do not replace that bracket calculation.',
14:' A logarithm of a dimensional quantity should be read aslog(m/m₀) with a fixed reference unitm₀; differentiation removes the constantlogm₀. If the reference or coefficient changes withℓ, an extra derivative appears. Piecewise threshold models also require separate one-sided derivatives and matching conditions, so a smooth identity cannot be applied across an unexplained discontinuity.',
15:' Near a real poleλ with massμ>0, the summandμ/(λ−z) tends to plus infinity from the left and minus infinity from the right. Between adjacent poles the derivative is a sum of positive terms, so continuity, strict monotonicity and these endpoint limits give exactly one zero. This is a finite rational-function theorem independent of the number137.',
16:' At aB-zero, B′=rφ_x cosφ because the termr′sinφ vanishes, whileA=r cosφ. Their ratio is therefore1/φ_x with no dependence on the amplitude r. This cancellation explains the positive mass formula. Real phase monotonicity on a finite interval alone does not establish a global upper-half-plane Herglotz representation.',
22:' The characteristic matters to the diagnostic example: in characteristic two the unsigned product2 vanishes, so that particular numerical failure disappears. The sign convention nevertheless remains the correct degree bookkeeping over arbitrary rings and is necessary for uniform compatibility with shifts, tensor products and cone triangles. A rational example avoids concealing the issue behind2=0.',
23:' Naturality can also be checked explicitly: replacingv byw(v) before currying is the same as precomposing the resulting mapV→Hom(W,U), and postcomposingF byU→U′ commutes with pointwise postcomposition. Thus the isomorphism respects the actual morphisms, which is the additional content of an adjunction beyond equality of two dimensions.',
26:' The same remainder identity certifies truncation error without a decimal approximation: afterN digits the omitted fraction is exactlyr_N/(b12^N), betweenzero and12^{-N}. For a repeating block oflengthh, multiplying by12^h and subtracting yields a rational denominator12^h−1. These two identities provide exact conversion in both directions.',
27:' The boundary inequalities also distinguish open disks from uncertain boundary roots. Equality in a coefficient comparison is not a validRouché certificate; it may place a root directly on the circle. For p(z)=z−1 at radiusone, the two coefficient magnitudes tie and the root lies on the boundary, exactly the situation strict dominance excludes.',
28:' A practical certificate may choose a fixedC rather than recomputingf′(x)^{-1} at each step. This makes the map and its derivative bound uniform on the entire interval. Newton iteration with a changing inverse may converge faster, but its guarantee must be established separately or shown to stay inside the same certified domain.'}
